IERUS specializes in technology research, testing, and implementation with core competencies in electromagnetics phenomenology, computational analytics (algorithm acceleration and machine learning), and weapon system engineering. IERUS develops value for our defense and commercial customers through accelerations of the technology life cycle: identifying, creating, transitioning, and producing technologies with integrity of purpose and product. IERUS offers competitive compensation packages, retirement options, and benefits packages. To learn more, please visit www.ierustech.com.
IERUS participates in projects that address weapon systems engineering and the application of advanced machine learning (ML) and artificial intelligence (AI) techniques as well as RF/Optical hardware prototyping and low rate production. We generally seek to apply agile development fundamentals across our corporate portfolio to accelerate technology development timelines. The end goal being early discovery, accelerated development, and high customer engagement.
Overview
As an Embedded Developer, you will be responsible for the design, development, and validation of embedded software within prototype RF systems and test apparatus used to validate radar processing algorithms. You will work within a multidisciplinary team of engineers to integrate embedded software and hardware components into a high-quality prototype.
Responsibilities
Design embedded interface architecture to system level requirements;
Implement firmware to interface PS/PL and other components;
Develop software to implement radar processing algorithms;
Generate interface documentation between software/firmware interface;
Develop user GUI and manual for test team to execute tests;
Analyze data to determine root cause of failure and generate reports/presentations; and
Work with engineers across IERUS locations to coordinate development capability to meet program development milestones.
Required Qualifications
Must have an Active Secret Clearance or higher;
Bachelor’s in electrical or computer engineering;
Knowledge of or experience in digital signal processing techniques;
Experience with Xilinx Vivado and Petalinux builds;
Experience with VHDL/Verilog;
Experience with C/C++;
Experience with MATLAB, Python, and/or other scripting languages;
Ability to travel up to 25%; and
Demonstrate effective verbal and written communication skills.
Preferred Requirements
Current SECRET security clearance.
Experience with realtime operating system embedded development;
Knowledge of data analysis techniques;
Experience with MOSA VPX chassis configuration and development;
Familiar with gnu compiler options and build tools (make, cmake, etc.); and
Active or ability to obtain TOP SECRET security clearance.
Location: Huntsville, AL
IERUS Technologies is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or veteran status, age, or any other federally protected class.
